{%- comment -%}
  Renders a product.metafields.custom.{key} value, or a visible-in-editor /
  invisible-in-production placeholder if it hasn't been filled in yet.

  Usage: {% render 'spec', product: product, key: 'thickness_mm', suffix: ' mm' %}
  Params: product (optional), key (required), prefix, suffix, label (override todo text)

  product falls back to settings.featured_product here rather than at each call
  site. Four storytelling sections each opened with their own copy of that same
  assign so they would work on the homepage as well as the PDP; resolving it in
  the one snippet they all funnel through means there is a single place where
  "which product is this page about" gets decided.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE METAFIELDS THIS THEME EXPECTS

  All under the `custom` namespace, on the product. This list is the manifest —
  it existed only implicitly before, scattered across the sections that call
  this snippet, so setting up a second product meant reading five section files
  to find out what to fill in.

    dimensions_unfolded   text     "6.5 x 5 ft"    fit comparator, specs
    dimensions_folded     text     "2.2 x 1.7 ft"  fit comparator, specs
    thickness_mm          number   rendered with " mm"
    weight_kg             number   rendered with " kg"
    panel_count           number   fit comparator, specs
    fold_time_seconds     number   fold sequence
    material              text     fit comparator, specs
    reversible            boolean  prints Yes / No, and false is a real answer
    care_note             text     fit comparator
    cleaning_note         text     safety panel
    test_report_status    text     safety panel
    test_report           file     safety panel, linked for download

  Any key left unset shows its label as a .bc-todo chip to a merchant in the
  theme editor and renders nothing at all to a customer, so a half-filled
  product is never a broken page.
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ctx = product | default: settings.featured_product
  assign mf = ctx.metafields.custom[key]
  assign todo_label = label

  case key
    when 'thickness_mm' 
      assign todo_label = todo_label | default: 'thickness'
    when 'dimensions_unfolded'
      assign todo_label = todo_label | default: 'unfolded size'
    when 'dimensions_folded'
      assign todo_label = todo_label | default: 'folded size'
    when 'weight_kg'
      assign todo_label = todo_label | default: 'weight'
    when 'panel_count'
      assign todo_label = todo_label | default: 'panel count'
    when 'fold_time_seconds'
      assign todo_label = todo_label | default: 'fold time'
    when 'material'
      assign todo_label = todo_label | default: 'material'
    else
      assign todo_label = todo_label | default: key | replace: '_', ' '
  endcase
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  Deliberately checking `mf.value == nil`, not `== blank`: Liquid's `blank`
  treats boolean false as blank, which would wrongly hide a real
  "reversible: false" value behind the missing-spec placeholder.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if mf.value == nil -%}<span class="bc-todo" data-todo="{{ key }}">{{ todo_label }}</span>{%- else -%}{{ prefix }}{% if mf.value == true %}Yes{% elsif mf.value == false %}No{% else %}{{ mf.value }}{% endif %}{{ suffix }}{%- endif -%}
